  "instance_name": "chicken_as_metaphor",
  "label": "Chicken as Metaphor for Women",
  "description": "The chicken is used as a crude metaphor to represent women in a degrading and violent context. This metaphor is not literal but symbolic, drawing on cultural associations of chickens as domesticated, easily controlled, and ultimately expendable animals. The use of this metaphor is a form of objectification that reduces women to their perceived role as objects of possession and consumption.",
